(6306703, 932327, 98339, '<td valign="top">Well, Kari..I know this is a little late...but I wanted to give you a comment at least...since I know it''s yours I''ll pull off the gloves (per say)<br/> <br/>I gave this a 7, great colors (nothing was pushed to much, has great balance), excellent detail in the ducks themselves...I think that just a "touch" more sharpening could have helped this a bit more (it seems a "little soft in the focus" a higher aperture (f/13/14) would have given you alot more feather detail), the tail of the one duck is cut off...that might have hurt you a bit (but that''s minor).  And finally, I don''t know why but duck/swan pictures don''t do so well in FS''s...if this had been a "wild life bird challenge" I think this would have placed very well....the tweaks I''m talking about are more "make it perfect" stuff....you get it...</td>', 'Well, Kari..I know this is a little late...but I wanted to give you a comment at least...since I know it''s yours I''ll pull off the gloves (per say) I gave this a 7, great colors (nothing was pushed to much, has great balance), excellent detail in the ducks themselves...I think that just a "touch" more sharpening could have helped this a bit more (it seems a "little soft in the focus" a higher aperture (f/13/14) would have given you alot more feather detail), the tail of the one duck is cut off...that might have hurt you a bit (but that''s minor).  And finally, I don''t know why but duck/swan pictures don''t do so well in FS''s...if this had been a "wild life bird challenge" I think this would have placed very well....the tweaks I''m talking about are more "make it perfect" stuff....you get it...', '2011-02-08 10:19:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(6306706, 931045, 48115, '<td valign="top">cant believe this is a cell phone shot! so much depth.. well done!</td>', 'cant believe this is a cell phone shot! so much depth.. well done!', '2011-02-08 10:25:12.000000', NULL, 0),
