(6306998, 931805, 76335, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by paulbtlw:</b></div><hr/><i>Critical stuff: Not much, perhaps I would like to have seen even more blur of the ground below their feet as the strong texture tends to pull the eye away from the stronger parts of the image.</i></td></tr></table> <br/>I respectfully disagree. The less-blurry ground helps anchor the scene. And too much blur down there would compete with the blur of the subjects, thereby reducing the effect. <br/> <br/>All of this misses the point, of course. Technical overanalysis aside, I think both Paul and I agree that this image is a winner.</td>', 'Originally posted by paulbtlw:Critical stuff: Not much, perhaps I would like to have seen even more blur of the ground below their feet as the strong texture tends to pull the eye away from the stronger parts of the image. I respectfully disagree. The less-blurry ground helps anchor the scene. And too much blur down there would compete with the blur of the subjects, thereby reducing the effect.  All of this misses the point, of course. Technical overanalysis aside, I think both Paul and I agree that this image is a winner.', '2011-02-08 17:33:13.000000', NULL, 0),
